 1. _1 names the first parameter:                            [1, 2].map { _1 * 2 } = [2, 4]
 2. it (Ruby 3.4) names it too:                              [1, 2].map { it * 2 } = [2, 4]
 3. _2 makes a two-parameter block:                          { _1 + _2 } = [3, 7], each_with_index.map { _1 * _2 } = [0, 2]
 4. it and a lone _1 take the whole pair, _2 splats it:      it.size [2], _1.size [2], _1 + _2 [3]
 5. arity and parameters:                                    proc { it } 1 [[:opt]], proc { _2 } 2 [[:opt, :_1], [:opt, :_2]], lambda { it } [[:req]]
 6. nested it is allowed, nested _1 is not:                  [[10, 20], [30]], SyntaxError
 7. it and _1 in one block:                                  SyntaxError
 8. it or _1 beside an ordinary |x|:                         SyntaxError, SyntaxError
 9. it is an ordinary name elsewhere, _1 is reserved:        a local it wins in a block: ["local"], no local: [10], _1 = 5: SyntaxError
10. it in a method body, no block:                           NameError: undefined local variable or method 'it' for main
